Pinyon Shift
  https://github.com/arcanite24/pinyon-shift
  https://github.com/arcanite24/shiftglue-sdk
  Copyright (c) 2026, Pinyon Shift contributors.
  BSD 3-Clause License: see LICENSE-Pinyon-Shift. Adapted here: the native
  ultrawide presentation and HUD viewport transforms (0063), the scRGB HDR
  presenter, highlight curve and HUD coverage shaders (0091), the contraction
  part of its macOS pixel-math tuning (0082), and the small code model on Linux
  x86-64 (0400). The already-loaded-only RenderDoc probe (0407) follows Pinyon
  Shift's approach; its DynamicLibrary integration and tests are authored here.

Downloaded at configure time, not stored in this repository (pinned revisions,
SHA-256 checked; each license is installed beside the GPU library):
  NVIDIA DLSS SDK headers and loader (NVIDIA's license in that SDK), for 0046.
  AMD FidelityFX SDK FSR 3.1 shaders (MIT), for 0072.
  SMAA by Jorge Jimenez et al., iryoku/smaa (MIT), for 0077.

ReIGlue contributors
  The changes on top of ReXGlue come from the Forza Horizon 1: ReImagined project
  (https://github.com/FH1-ReImagined/ForzaHorizon1-ReImagined); the first ones
  were written for RecompiledHaloReach. Authors, as each commit records:
    Maximiliano Militzer (Dyotson)
    Sean O’Connor (soconnor0919)
  Thanks also to the players who reported problems and sent logs; the issues the
  commit messages cite (#N, Forza Horizon 1: ReImagined's issues) name them.

